tays allocated forever. That seems problematic: we cannot change which vehicle is allocated to a candidate. The allocate action only adds vehicle_allocated if not already allocated. There is no action to remove vehicle_allocated. So a candidate once allocated a vehicle keeps it allocated forever. Therefore we cannot reassign vehicles. So we must allocate each candidate a distinct vehicle from the start and never change.)
(Thus we need to allocate distinct vehicles to each candidate: oa, da, sa, sb each need a vehicle allocated. We have three vehicles only. But goal requires vehicle_allocated oa, da, sa, sb all true. That's four vehicles needed. However we have only three vehicles. This seems impossible unless some candidate can share vehicle? But as argued, vehicle_allocated is monotonic (only added). So can't have more allocated candidates than vehicles.)
(Let's double-check init: vehicle_allocated oa true, vehicle_allocated sa true. No vehicle_allocated for da or sb. Goal wants vehicle_allocated da and sb true. So we need to allocate vehicles to da and sb. We have vuB available, vuA allocated to oa, vuG allocated to sa. So we can allocate vuB to da (makes vehicle_allocated da true). For sb we need another vehicle, but none left. However maybe we can allocate vuA to sb and keep oa allocated? But oa already allocated vuA; cannot allocate another vehicle to oa because vehicle_allocated oa already true, but we could still allocate another vehicle? The allocate action precondition includes not vehicle_allocated ?candidate. So if oa already vehicle_allocated true, we cannot allocate another vehicle to oa. So we cannot shift.)
