(Thus we can reuse vehicle after dispatching da, because vehicle_allocated da remains true, but vehicle_available becomes true again after dispatch, allowing reallocation.)
(Thus we can allocate vuB to da, dispatch da (making vehicle_available vuB true again while da still allocated), then allocate vuB to sb, making vehicle_allocated sb true and vehicle_available vuB false again. At the end, both da and sb have vehicle_allocated true (same vehicle), vehicle_available vuB false. However goal also wants vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha and vehicle_unit_gamma. Those will be available after dispatching oa and sa. So final vehicle availability: vuA and vuG available (since dispatched oa and sa), vuB not available (since allocated to both da and sb). Goal does not require vehicle_available vuB, so it's fine.)
